Implementing a Netfilter hook in Rust requires using the **Linux Kernel Module (LKM)** framework. Since the Linux kernel is written in C, you will need to use the `kernel` crate provided by the **Rust-for-Linux** project.

### Prerequisites

1.  **Kernel Version:** You need a recent kernel (6.1+) that supports Rust.
2.  **Toolchain:** You must have the `rustc` compiler that matches your kernel version and the `bindgen` tool.
3.  **Environment:** It is highly recommended to use the official [Rust-for-Linux](https://github.com/Rust-for-Linux/linux) tree rather than trying to build a standalone module against a generic kernel, as the abstraction layers (the `kernel` crate) are built into the kernel source.

---

### Implementation Guide

In Netfilter, you register a "hook" function that the kernel calls whenever a packet hits a specific chain (e.g., `NF_INET_PRE_ROUTING`).

#### 1. The Hook Function
The hook function must match a specific signature. It receives the packet (sk_buff) and returns a verdict (e.g., `NF_ACCEPT` or `NF_DROP`).

#### 2. The Code Example
Below is a conceptual implementation. *Note: Because the Rust-for-Linux API is evolving rapidly, some function names may vary slightly depending on your specific kernel branch.*

```rust
//! A simple Netfilter hook in Rust that logs packets.

use kernel::prelude::*;
use kernel::net::{netfilter, nf_hook_ops};

module! {
    type: MyNetfilterModule,
    name: "rust_netfilter",
    author: "Your Name",
    description: "A simple Rust Netfilter hook",
    license: "GPL",
}

struct MyNetfilterModule {
    // We store the hook operations here to keep them in memory
    _ops: nf_hook_ops,
}

impl kernel::Module for MyNetfilterModule {
    fn init(_module: &'static ThisModule) -> Result<Self> {
        pr_info!("Rust Netfilter module loading...\n");

        // Define the hook operations
        let mut ops = nf_hook_ops::new();

        // 1. Set the hook function
        ops.hook = Some(packet_hook);

        // 2. Set the hook point (Pre-Routing)
        ops.hook_num = netfilter::NF_INET_PRE_ROUTING;

        // 3. Set priority (0 is standard)
        ops.pf = netfilter::NFPROTO_IPV4;
        ops.priority = 0;

        // Register the hook with the kernel
        unsafe {
            netfilter::nf_register_net_hook(&kernel::net::init_net(), &ops);
        }

        Ok(MyNetfilterModule { _ops: ops })
    }
}

impl Drop for MyNetfilterModule {
    fn drop(&mut self) {
        pr_info!("Rust Netfilter module unloading...\n");
        // Unregister the hook to prevent kernel panic on unload
        unsafe {
            netfilter::nf_unregister_net_hook(&kernel::net::init_net(), &self._ops);
        }
    }
}

