To make a physics-based character with networked gadgets, you need to move away from "local" interaction and move toward "ownership-based" interaction. 

In PUN 2, the most important rule for physics is: **Only the owner of the object should calculate its physics.** If everyone tries to move a gadget, it will jitter violently.

Here is the architecture for your expanded `NetworkInteractable`.

### 1. The NetworkInteractable Script
This script extends `XRGrabInteractable`. Its primary job is to handle **Ownership Transfer**. When a player grabs a gadget, they must become the "owner" of that object in Photon so their physics calculations are sent to everyone else.

```csharp
using UnityEngine;
using UnityEngine.XR.Interaction.Toolkit;
using Photon.Pun;
using Photon.Realtime;

public class NetworkInteractable : XRGrabInteractable
{
    private PhotonView photonView;

    protected override void Awake()
    {
        base.Awake();
        photonView = GetComponent<PhotonView>();

        if (photonView == null)
        {
            Debug.LogError($"NetworkInteractable on {gameObject.name} requires a PhotonView component!");
        }
    }

    protected override void OnSelectEntered(SelectEnterEventArgs args)
    {
        // 1. Request ownership of the object so we can move it physically
        if (photonView != null && !photonView.IsMine)
        {
            photonView.RequestOwnership();
        }

        base.OnSelectEntered(args);
    }

    protected override void OnSelectExited(SelectExitEventArgs args)
    {
        base.OnSelectExited(args);

        // Optional: You can release ownership here or keep it until someone else grabs it.
        // Usually, keeping it until the next grab is smoother for physics.
    }

    // This ensures that if we aren't the owner, we don't fight the network sync
    protected override void OnActivate()
    {
        // Only the owner should trigger the "Use" logic (e.g., firing a blaster)
        if (photonView != null && photonView.IsMine)
        {
            base.OnActivate();
        }
        else
        {
            // If a non-owner activates it, tell the owner to activate it via RPC
            photonView.RPC("RPC_Activate", RpcTarget.Owner);
        }
    }

    [PunRPC]
    public void RPC_Activate()
    {
        // This is called on the owner's machine, which then triggers the actual logic
        base.OnActivate();
    }
}
```

